<section>
<p>Effective date: October 19, 2026</p>
</section>

<section id="scope">
<h2>Who this policy covers</h2>
<p>This policy applies to beverified.org ("BeVerified", "we", "us"). It explains what happens to information when you visit the site, follow a link from it or email us. It does not cover the websites of providers we review or any other site we link to.</p>
</section>

<section id="not-collected">
<h2>What we don't collect</h2>
<p>BeVerified is a static website. Unless you accept analytics (see below), we don't collect, store or sell any personal data about you. In particular:</p>
<ul>
<li>We don't run heatmaps, session recording or advertising pixels.</li>
<li>We don't have user accounts, sign-up forms, comment sections or newsletters.</li>
<li>Fonts, images and our own scripts are served from our own domain.</li>
<li>We don't buy, sell, rent or share personal data with anyone.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="analytics">
<h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
<p>We use Google Analytics 4, a service of Google, to count visits and see which pages are useful. It only runs if you click "Accept" in the banner. If you decline or ignore the banner, no analytics script is loaded and no analytics cookies are set.</p>
<p>If you accept, Google Analytics sets cookies (such as <code>_ga</code>) and receives technical data: pages viewed, referring page, approximate location derived from your IP address, browser and device type. We use this data in aggregate only, to improve the site. Google processes it under its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>, and data may be transferred to the United States.</p>
<p>We store your choice in your browser's local storage under the name <code>bv-analytics-consent</code> so we don't ask again. To change your mind, clear this site's data in your browser and the banner will appear on your next visit. The legal basis for analytics is your consent; you can withdraw it at any time this way.</p>
</section>

<section id="hosting">
<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. Like any web host, GitHub may process technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the page requested in order to deliver the site and protect it against abuse. GitHub processes that data under its own <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">privacy statement</a>. We don't receive those server logs and can't use them to identify visitors.</p>
</section>

<section id="links">
<h2>Links to other websites</h2>
<p>Reviews link to provider websites and other sources. Some of those links may be affiliate links, which means the destination site or an affiliate network may learn that you arrived from BeVerified, usually through a parameter in the link. Once you leave our site, the other site's privacy policy and cookie rules apply, not ours. We don't control and aren't responsible for how third-party sites handle your data.</p>
</section>

<section id="email">
<h2>If you email us</h2>
<p>If you write to <a href="mailto:support@beverified.org">support@beverified.org</a>, we receive your email address, your name if you include it and whatever you put in the message. We use that only to read and answer your message, for example to handle a correction request or a profile claim. We keep the correspondence only as long as we need it for that purpose, and we don't add you to any mailing list.</p>
<p>Please don't send us identity documents, passwords or other sensitive personal information. We don't need them and won't ask for them.</p>
</section>

<section id="rights">
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live, laws such as the EU and UK GDPR or US state privacy laws give you rights over your personal data, including the right to access it, correct it or have it deleted. Since we don't collect data from site visitors, in most cases we will simply have nothing on file about you. If you have emailed us, you can ask us to delete that correspondence by writing to the address above. You also have the right to complain to your local data protection authority.</p>
</section>

<section id="children">
<h2>Children</h2>
<p>BeVerified is written for businesses and professionals. It is not aimed at children, and we don't knowingly receive personal data from anyone under 16.</p>
</section>

<section id="changes">
<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If the way the site works changes, for example if we ever add analytics or a contact form, we will update this page before that change goes live and change the effective date above.</p>
</section>

<section id="contact">
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:support@beverified.org">support@beverified.org</a>.</p>
</section>
